# CalculatorSoup

> CalculatorSoup is a free library of online calculators for math, finance, time and date, unit conversion, statistics, construction, geometry, physics and health. Many calculators show the formulas and step-by-step work used to get the answer.

Last updated: 2026-10-05

## About the Site

- **Shows the work:** Many calculators show the formula and intermediate steps along with the answer. Tools like the Fractions and Long Division calculators are useful for checking student work or explaining how a result was found.
- **Input formats:** Most calculators accept whole numbers and decimals, and many accept fractions or E-notation (e.g., `1.23E7`).
- **No account required:** Calculators are free to use without signing up or logging in.
- **URL structure:** Most calculators are at `https://www.calculatorsoup.com/calculators/[category]/[tool-name].php`.
- **Pre-filled links:** Many calculators accept inputs as URL parameters and calculate when `action=solve` is included. Parameter names differ from one calculator to another. Example: `https://www.calculatorsoup.com/calculators/math/fractions.php?n_1=3&d_1=4&operator=add&n_2=1&d_2=2&action=solve` calculates 3/4 + 1/2.
- **Shareable answer links:** After a calculation, many calculators can generate a link that keeps the input values and results.
- **Formulas:** Most calculator pages include the formulas used. Separate formula pages: [Statistics Formulas](https://www.calculatorsoup.com/calculators/statistics/statistics-formulas.php), [Future Value Formula](https://www.calculatorsoup.com/calculators/financial/future-value-formula.php), [Present Value Formula](https://www.calculatorsoup.com/calculators/financial/present-value-formula.php).

